## What OT visibility must provide

An IT asset tool usually relies on agents or credentialed scans. Neither works well in OT: PLCs cannot run agents, and an aggressive scan can crash an old controller. OT visibility must work mostly **passively**, by observing traffic, and must understand **industrial protocols** well enough to extract details such as:

- vendor, model, firmware version, serial number and rack/slot modules of each controller;
- which hosts talk to which, over which protocol, and with which commands (read, write, program download, mode change);
- which devices act as engineering stations, HMIs, historians or I/O;
- known vulnerabilities that apply to the discovered firmware.

This inventory feeds almost every other control: zone design, firewall rules, ISE profiling, vulnerability management and incident response.
